{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Main manuscript analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is the public-facing analysis workflow.\n",
    "\n",
    "It uses only the four manuscript event-window files in\n",
    "`data/manuscript_storm_events/`. The complete long-term monitoring archive is\n",
    "not required and is not included in this repository.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "Install the repository in editable mode once with `pip install -e .`, then run\n",
    "the notebook from the repository root.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "from wq_preprocessing.config import DEFAULT_CONFIG\n",
    "from wq_preprocessing.data_io import load_manuscript_events\n",
    "from wq_preprocessing.experiment import run_fixed_rule_experiment\n",
    "from wq_preprocessing.hydrologic_phase import classify_all_storms\n",
    "from wq_preprocessing.temporal_aggregation import resample_all_storms_dict\n",
    "\n",

   # Find repository root whether notebook is launched from root or /analysis
   PROJECT_ROOT = Path.cwd()
   if PROJECT_ROOT.name == "analysis":
       PROJECT_ROOT = PROJECT_ROOT.parent
   
   DATA_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / "data" / "manuscript_storm_events"
   RESULTS = PROJECT_ROOT / "results"
   RESULTS.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
   
   print("Project root:", PROJECT_ROOT)
   print("Data directory:", DATA_DIR)
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load the four manuscript storm events\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "all_storms = load_manuscript_events(\"data/manuscript_storm_events\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for storm_id, item in all_storms.items():\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        storm_id,\n",
    "        item[\"metadata\"][\"site\"],\n",
    "        item[\"data\"].index.min(),\n",
    "        item[\"data\"].index.max(),\n",
    "        len(item[\"data\"])\n",
    "    )\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Hydrologic-phase classification\n",
    "\n",
    "The radar-derived distance signal is inverted and normalized internally so that\n",
    "larger values represent higher water level. The resulting `Stage_smoothed`\n",
    "series is used for the hydrologic-phase analysis and hydrology-informed\n",
    "gap-filling methods.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "classified_storms = classify_all_storms(all_storms)\n",
    "\n",
    "for storm_id, item in classified_storms.items():\n",
    "    print(storm_id, item[\"info\"])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Primary fixed-rule experiment\n",
    "\n",
    "This reproduces the primary five gap-filling methods and nine\n",
    "denoising/correction methods using the fixed experiment configuration.\n",
    "\n",
    "The additional Moving Mean, \u0394H-weighted, and HPWI gap-filling methods were added\n",
    "later in the study and are implemented in `src/wq_preprocessing/gap_filling.py`.\n",
    "The archived result tables used in the paper should be placed in `results/`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "raw_results = run_fixed_rule_experiment(\n",
    "    all_storms=all_storms,\n",
    "    config=DEFAULT_CONFIG,\n",
    "    checkpoint_dir=RESULTS / \"checkpoints\",\n",
    "    checkpoint_every=500,\n",
    "    verbose=True,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_results.to_csv(RESULTS / \"results_fixed_rule_raw.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "raw_results.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Temporal aggregation\n",
    "\n",
    "The manuscript sensitivity analysis evaluates 30-min and 1-h temporal\n",
    "aggregation relative to the native event series. The helper below reproduces\n",
    "the event aggregation. Frequency-aware block-missingness helpers are provided\n",
    "in `temporal_aggregation.py`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "storms_30min = resample_all_storms_dict(all_storms, \"30min\")\n",
    "storms_1h = resample_all_storms_dict(all_storms, \"1h\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Native:\", {k: len(v[\"data\"]) for k,v in all_storms.items()})\n",
    "print(\"30 min:\", {k: len(v[\"data\"]) for k,v in storms_30min.items()})\n",
    "print(\"1 h:\", {k: len(v[\"data\"]) for k,v in storms_1h.items()})\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Figure reproduction\n",
    "\n",
    "All plotting code has deliberately been moved out of this notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "Use:\n",
    "\n",
    "`figures/figure_reproduction.ipynb`\n",
    "\n",
    "after the analysis result CSV files have been generated.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
